WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.535
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.903
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.606
between Pret A Manger
in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.108
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.878
OK, slight problem.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.481
There's only one Pret in
LA, and it's at the airport.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:17.117
And due to the pandemic,
it's currently closed.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.351
The Pret, not the airport.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.653
Luckily, there's plenty
of Prets in New York City,

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.023
where I have many colleagues
and casual acquaintances

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.091
who would love to help me out.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.760
Everyone, meet Irene.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:27.994
Hi, everyone.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.297
Sorry I'm not Joe, but I'll
try not to let you down.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:35.568
I did ask if I could wear one of these,

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.403
but they said no.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.205
So you're stuck with my face. Sorry.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.510
Here is everything you
will only find on the menu

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.944
at a UK Pret A Manger.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.881
And here's everything you
can only find on the menu

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.182
at a US Pret.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.383
We'll start with the drinks.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.519
We have quite a few exclusive
drink options in the UK,

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.255
starting with this one, a turmeric latte,

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.890
and also a matcha latte,

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.725
both of which are made with coconut milk

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.692
instead of regular milk.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.894
I'm going to try the turmeric latte,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.163
just because the color is so vivid

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.031
and a little bit off-putting.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.300
I want to find out if it
tastes as bad as it looks.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:09.936
Oh, man.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.772
No, no. It tastes like a chicken korma.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.641
Which is great, don't get me wrong,

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.943
but I don't want to drink
that from a coffee shop.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.745
Then we have iced
versions of both of these.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.748
So we have an iced turmeric
latte and an iced matcha latte.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.016
Next up we've got some frappés.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:26.052
We have a classic frappé
here, which is just coffee,

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.221
and then we have a chocolate
frappé at the back as well.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.422
Then we have some bottled and canned

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.457
exclusive drinks as well.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.724
For example, apple juice.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.860
Sparkling lemon and rhubarb drink.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.196
Then we have a sparkling ginger drink.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.631
And over here we have a
sparkling apple drink.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.801
And, finally, a sparkling
grape and elderflower drink.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.837
Our exclusive drinks include

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:47.307
an organic, single-origin Ethiopia coffee,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:51.778
salted caramel latte, salted
caramel hot chocolate,

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.148
s'mores hot chocolate, cold-brew coffee,

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:58.485
iced green tea, classic lemonade,

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.086
grapefruit sparkling water,

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.888
and raspberry-lime sparkling water.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.224
If you want to start your day
off with a Pret breakfast,

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.758
here are some options
you'll find in the UK.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.794
We'll start with a
classic, which is porridge.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.462
In the UK, you can get
porridge three ways.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.864
You can get it plain, like we have here,

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.366
you can get it with a
fruit compote on the top,

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.602
or you can get it with
cranberries and seeds.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.537
A Very Berry croissant.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:18.371
Croissant?

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.239
Croissant.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:19.973
Croissant.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.440
Croissant.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.742
At the front here we have
a Very Berry croissant,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.644
which is a kind of, like, folded croissant

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.179
with some berry jam in the middle.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.847
At the back here we have a ham, bacon,

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.215
cheese, and tomato croissant.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.583
Double the pork, double the fun.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.818
Then we have some breakfast-roll options,

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.187
such as this one, which
is a sausage and egg roll.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.588
Then we have three breakfast baguettes.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.857
Here, we have an egg and bacon baguette.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.260
In the middle, we have an
egg and salmon baguette.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.862
And then, over here, we have
an egg and avocado baguette.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.063
On top of this, there's a couple of bits

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.332
that we couldn't get today
because of a reduced menu.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.602
These include a veggie
roll, a five berry bowl,

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.504
and a Mango &amp; Banana Sunshine Bowl,

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.705
which sounds just delightful.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.275
Only exclusive breakfast
item we were able to get

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.877
is the shakshuka frittata.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.546
But the other menu items

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:02.348
are the egg and bacon brioche roll,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.417
an egg and cheddar brioche roll,

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.653
an egg white Greek frittata,

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.821
a ham and spinach frittata,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.490
a Morning Glory muffin,

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.559
and an everything bagel,

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.527
and an energy bagel.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.129
We have two exclusive salads in the UK.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.031
This one is the tuna Nicoise,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.066
and this one is the
Chef's Italian Chicken.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.368
We have three exclusive salads.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.871
The first is the chicken avocado salad.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.272
This is the chicken Caesar salad.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.408
Joe: Salads, ugh!
Irene: Chipotle chicken salad

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.509
is my favorite.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.044
Now we're on to sandwiches and wraps.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.612
We have quite a few exclusive sandwiches

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.746
and wraps in the UK.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:34.981
We have a personal favorite of mine,

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.350
which is a smoked salmon
and cream cheese sandwich.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.018
This one here is a jambon-beurre,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.253
which is just a very simple

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.589
ham, butter, and pickle sandwich.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.224
Then we have some baguette
options, including this one,

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.392
which is an Avo, Olives &amp; Toms baguette.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.562
That's avocado, olives, and
tomatoes, for the uninitiated.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.065
Here we have a Posh
Cheddar &amp; Pickle sandwich.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:52.899
Two things to note here.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.567
One, I'm not sure why this is posh.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.302
Two, when we say pickle in this context,

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.171
we don't mean gherkins.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.773
We actually mean pickle,
which is a British condiment

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.842
made with kind of, like, pickle juices,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.844
but also some other
vegetables in there as well.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:06.779
The last baguette we were
able to get today is this one,

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.748
which is a chicken Caesar
and bacon baguette.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.049
Then we have a couple of wrap options,

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.485
such as this one, which is
a hoisin duck salad wrap,

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.154
and this one, which is a
hummus and chipotle wrap.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.656
The ones we were unable
to get today include

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.890
a tuna and cucumber sandwich

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.759
and a Brie, tomato, and basil baguette.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.894
Our sandwiches and wraps include

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.796
the cheddar and tomato,

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.132
chipotle and chicken avocado wrap,

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.001
Bang Bang Chicken Wrap.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.938
It's not spicy but has,
like, a kick to it.

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.373
This is good. I might start getting it.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:36.309
The next ones we have
up on our exclusive list

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.978
is the pesto chicken flatbread.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:42.315
This is the falafel and hummus flatbread,

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.983
pesto caprese baguette,

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:47.287
and the balsamic chicken
and mozzarella baguette.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.889
Now, usually I'd have a
bunch of exclusive soups

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:50.990
to show you from a UK Pret.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.126
However, they've reduced the
menu because of the pandemic.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.594
Here's what we'd normally be able to find.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.129
A chicken laksa,

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.131
a chicken, broccoli, and brown rice,

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.599
chicken pot pie soup,

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:00.600
miso soup,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.701
pea and mint soup,

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.169
chicken katsu curry soup,

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.370
mushroom risotto soup,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.805
and a red Thai veg soup.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:10.143
So, our soup options
include the Moroccan lentil,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.110
turkey chili,

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.480
and the turmeric chicken and farro.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.382
Far-oh? Fa – I think it's farro.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:17.950
They came with all this bread, though,

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.018
which is pretty fun.

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.120
And it's the good kind of bread, too.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.689
You know bread is good when it comes

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.957
in, like, a triangular shape.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.160
That's just been my
observation over the years.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.895
Oh, that's good for cold soup.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:35.301
Narrator: Live from New York,
it's "What Shape Is It?"

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:36.502
[game-show music]

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.974
Corner, corner, triangular.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.976
Yeah, Irene, I believe that's a rhombus.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:44.811
It's not a triangle.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:48.214
Triangle, to my understanding,
means three sides, right?

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:48.848
Right?

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.016
Joe, you're a lot closer with a rhombus,

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.452
but I personally am gonna
go with parallelogram.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.220
[game-show music]

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.321
Narrator: "What Shape Is It?" is filmed

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.989
in front of a live studio audience.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.624
I think this is a triangular shape.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.793
But I guess fine. It's
like a diamond shape.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.528
But I'm just saying that when bread comes

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:06.432
in, like, a geometric
shape, it's good bread.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.835
The fanciest restaurants I've gone to,

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:11.404
they have bread that's shaped like this.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.573
Or, like, even sharper.

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.641
What kind of bread are
you eating that's sharp?

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.943
Where are you going?

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.444
Then, finally, we're on to the snacks.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.012
At a UK Pret, you will be able to find

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.215
some mature cheddar and red onion crisps,

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.850
some smoked chipotle crisps,

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.451
some sweet and salt popcorn,

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.719
these little hazelnut truffles,

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:29.055
Pret A Mango, and a chocolate brownie bar.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.691
[mocking Joe] Kettle corn?
What even is kettle corn?

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:34.227
What even – what even is kettle corn?

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:37.230
We are so exclusive, we
were only able to get

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.600
one of our exclusive snacks,
which is kettle corn.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.803
So, this was the only exclusive
snack we were able to get,

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:47.440
but the other items on
the menu are the nut bar,

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.577
popcorn bar, Pret bar,
and some omega-3 mix.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:55.081
Let's start with the drinks.

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:58.017
In the UK, the majority of hot
drinks only come in one size,

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.852
which is 12 ounces.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.854
Pret says this is to optimize efficiency

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.389
and to keep things simple for customers.

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.591
However, there are two
exceptions to this rule.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:09.061
Firstly, if you order a
flat white from a UK Pret,

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:11.063
it's served as an 8-ounce drink.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:14.100
Then, if you order an
espresso or a macchiato,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.669
it comes in one of these
adorable little 4-ounce cups.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:18.004
All right. So, in the US,

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:20.473
our hot coffees come in three sizes.

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:22.942
Small,

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:25.978
medium,

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:27.113
and large.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.848
It's ridiculous.

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:31.250
But we also have some
exceptions to the rules.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:35.621
Our flat white is only
served as an 8-ounce drink.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:39.392
But our macchiato is 4
ounces, like the UK's.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:42.328
And our espresso is
actually just 2 ounces.

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.630
I guess they're trying to
limit our caffeine intake.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:45.264
Maybe.

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:46.966
Harry: We're going to measure
our largest black coffee

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.100
to find out if you're actually getting

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.635
as much as you're told you are.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:53.439
So, to Pret's credit,
that is exactly 12 ounces.

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:58.211
We are not getting as much
coffee as they say we are.

00:07:58.211 --> 00:08:00.813
But ... maybe that's a good thing?

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.215
20's kind of a lot.

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:04.684
Joe: Not getting as much coffee
as advertised, huh, Irene?

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:06.018
Welcome to "Food Wars."

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.053
What about iced coffees?

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:09.055
Well, in the UK, these
also just come in one size.

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:11.557
Well, over here, we can
get iced black coffee

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:14.427
as either a 16- or

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.729
24-ounce serving.

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.431
That's a lot of coffee.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:21.234
I don't get people who drink black coffee.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:22.802
Harry: We're both gonna
measure our largest

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:25.705
iced black coffee to find
out what they come to.

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:27.240
[coffee gurgling]

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.976
So, once again, this came
to exactly 12 ounces.

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:33.779
So, the iced coffee is also
not the advertised amount.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.548
It's supposed to be 24 ounces,

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:38.351
but it looks like it's only about 21.

00:08:38.451 --> 00:08:42.255
It's an international coffee conspiracy!

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:44.657
Season two, we're still dealing with this!

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:46.859
I mean, is someone gonna
do something about this?

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:49.662
Once again, maybe not a bad thing.

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.798
I feel like a lot of people are
going to disagree with that.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:54.934
Do you need this much
caffeine in your life?

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:56.435
Probably.

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.938
I don't know if Joe or Harry
drinks this much coffee.

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:00.740
I feel like Joe might. He –

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.943
he seems like he would.
He has that energy.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.178
Joe just looks like he just drinks, like,

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:07.980
five cups of black coffee a day,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.416
and then he's up at, like,
2 a.m., just, like, haunted.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:11.984
Joe: Mm-hmm. Yes, I do.

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:13.419
I drink a lot of coffee.

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:15.521
I should say that it's only April

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:17.924
and I've already passed three
kidney stones this year.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.425
What about some of the food options?

00:09:19.425 --> 00:09:21.561
This is an egg salad
sandwich from a UK Pret.

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:23.729
We're going to weigh this one
to see how much it comes to.

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:26.332
Irene: It's exactly 250 grams.

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:27.833
Maybe our eggs are heavier.

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:30.436
It's all those preservatives.

00:09:30.436 --> 00:09:31.938
If you were raised here,
you wouldn't be worried.

00:09:32.138 --> 00:09:33.506
We should probably be worried.

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:40.646
It's not that good. But I'm hungry.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:44.383
Joe: ♪ Egg salad is gross! ♪

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:45.751
Like, it genuinely doesn't taste good,

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.453
but I'm just taking bites of it.

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:48.554
So, that was a classic sandwich,

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:49.722
but what about a baguette?

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.958
This is a ham and cheese
baguette from a UK Pret.

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:53.359
So, our UK ham and cheese baguette

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:54.927
came to exactly 200 grams.

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:58.831
Well, here's our famous
ham and cheese baguette.

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:02.068
It says it should weigh 251 grams.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:07.840
It's exactly 251 grams.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.075
That's impressive.

00:10:09.809 --> 00:10:10.776
That's actually kind of scary.

00:10:10.776 --> 00:10:13.079
I know it should weigh exactly
the amount it says it should,

00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:15.448
but, like, it's kind of
cool when it actually does.

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.116
Next up, we've got this muffin.

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:19.485
This is a double berry
muffin from a UK Pret,

00:10:19.485 --> 00:10:20.419
which is a blueberry muffin

00:10:20.419 --> 00:10:22.388
with some extra blueberry
compote in the middle.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:26.258
All right, so, we have our
classic blueberry muffin,

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:29.061
without the extra compote in the middle.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.364
Harry: Let's find out how much it weighs.

00:10:33.332 --> 00:10:35.501
Do you know the muffin man?

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:36.736
The muffin man?

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:37.870
The muffin man!

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:40.573
Yes, I know the muffin man
who lives on Drury Lane.

00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:41.540
God, I love "Shrek."

00:10:42.108 --> 00:10:43.776
Could we get a Harry Shrek?

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:46.512
Can we get Harry's face
turned into Shrek, please?

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:47.947
You know I've never seen "Shrek"?

00:10:48.414 --> 00:10:50.316
My surname's an anagram of Shrek.

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:55.655
Let's start with the
nutritional information

00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:56.756
for some of Pret's coffees.

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:59.892
An Americano in the UK contains nothing.

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:02.261
There's no calories, fat,
sugar or salt in here.

00:11:02.361 --> 00:11:03.996
So, that's also true here.

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:06.666
It's even the same for our largest size.

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:08.467
20 ounces of US Americano

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:10.870
has basically no nutritional value.

00:11:11.037 --> 00:11:13.072
There are more notable differences
when milk gets involved.

00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:14.674
Take the flat white, for example.

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:16.575
In the UK, one of these is 80 calories.

00:11:16.909 --> 00:11:20.913
OK, well, in the US, a flat
white contains 90 calories,

00:11:20.913 --> 00:11:23.649
but it apparently has absolutely no fat,

00:11:23.649 --> 00:11:26.585
while the UK version has 2.9 grams of fat.

00:11:26.886 --> 00:11:29.155
So, this is because Pret's US website

00:11:29.155 --> 00:11:31.991
bases the nutritionals for
its coffees on skim milk,

00:11:31.991 --> 00:11:35.161
whereas the UK bases its info on 2% milk.

00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:37.096
If we add the nutritional info

00:11:37.096 --> 00:11:39.832
for an 8-ounce serving of
whole milk from a US Pret,

00:11:39.832 --> 00:11:42.201
the flat white looks more like this.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.839
What about the least healthy
drink on the UK menu?

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:48.941
Well, it's actually this,
the chocolate frappé.

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:51.177
One of these contains 439 calories,

00:11:51.177 --> 00:11:53.345
which is a little over a
fifth of your daily allowance.

00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:54.847
More alarmingly, this also contains

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:56.749
your entire daily allowance of sugar.

00:11:57.016 --> 00:11:59.952
So, this is our least healthy drink.

00:11:59.952 --> 00:12:02.788
It's a salted caramel hot chocolate.

00:12:02.788 --> 00:12:05.524
Pound for pound, it
actually has less calories

00:12:05.524 --> 00:12:07.159
than the UK's chocolate frappé,

00:12:07.159 --> 00:12:09.195
with only 410 calories

00:12:09.195 --> 00:12:12.431
compared to their 439 calories.

00:12:12.498 --> 00:12:15.134
So while the UK's drink
is limited to one size,

00:12:15.134 --> 00:12:18.871
in the US we have a second size option.

00:12:18.871 --> 00:12:21.307
This brings the calories up to 700

00:12:21.307 --> 00:12:24.910
and also takes the sugar up to 113 grams,

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.913
which is more than double
your daily recommended limit.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.316
Why do they let
us add so much sugar?

00:12:30.316 --> 00:12:31.984
And you can take it even further

00:12:31.984 --> 00:12:34.553
by adding a syrup to your drink.

00:12:34.553 --> 00:12:36.922
One pump of Pret's
toasted marshmallow syrup

00:12:36.922 --> 00:12:39.792
will add another 24 grams
of sugar to your drink,

00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:45.164
bringing the total to 274% of
your daily sugar allowance.

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:47.533
Oh, God, that's sweet.

00:12:49.702 --> 00:12:52.505
That's the thing. I like my coffee sweet.

00:12:52.505 --> 00:12:54.006
Like, I only drink sweet coffee,

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:55.241
so this is right up my lane.

00:12:55.241 --> 00:12:57.943
Like, it has to be so sweet it hurts me.

00:12:57.977 --> 00:12:59.178
Yeah, hot chocolate is what that's called.

00:12:59.178 --> 00:13:00.379
What you want is a hot chocolate.

00:13:00.446 --> 00:13:03.349
Mm. You're right, this is not coffee.

00:13:03.415 --> 00:13:04.416
It's good, though.

00:13:06.585 --> 00:13:07.820
What about some food options?

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:10.089
In the UK, the most calorific
sandwich is this one,

00:13:10.089 --> 00:13:11.590
the Classic Super Club.

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.526
There is chicken, bacon, tomato,

00:13:13.526 --> 00:13:15.094
lettuce, mayo, and seasoning in here,

00:13:15.094 --> 00:13:17.930
and it leaves the total calories at 526.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.466
That's lower than our
most calorific sandwich,

00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:23.669
chicken and bacon, which
is one of my favorites.

00:13:23.669 --> 00:13:26.138
One of these contains 570 calories

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:29.175
and also half of your
daily sodium allowance.

00:13:29.175 --> 00:13:30.843
I did not know that.

00:13:31.043 --> 00:13:34.180
But this isn't the most
calorific thing on the menu.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:37.216
That would be the falafel
and red peppers wrap,

00:13:37.216 --> 00:13:39.385
which we weren't able to get.

00:13:39.385 --> 00:13:41.754
But it has 630 calories,

00:13:41.754 --> 00:13:43.789
which is more than any
other hot food item.

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:45.124
Now, unusually for "Food Wars,"

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:46.392
the highest-calorie item in the UK

00:13:46.392 --> 00:13:48.961
is actually more calorific than
the biggest one in America.

00:13:48.961 --> 00:13:50.796
For us, it's the Swedish
meatball hot wrap,

00:13:50.796 --> 00:13:53.265
which comes in at 661 calories.

00:13:53.265 --> 00:13:54.900
The calorie count might
not be super high for this,

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.803
but there is also 81% of your
daily saturated fat in here.

00:14:00.773 --> 00:14:03.108
For the most part, Pret
uses natural ingredients

00:14:03.108 --> 00:14:04.743
for things where possible.

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.579
However, after combing through
their ingredients lists

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:08.113
in the UK and the US, we did find

00:14:08.113 --> 00:14:09.248
one or two things to look out for.

00:14:09.448 --> 00:14:10.816
For example, caramel color.

00:14:10.816 --> 00:14:12.151
It's used in a range of Pret products,

00:14:12.151 --> 00:14:14.253
from the dressing that
they put on their salads

00:14:14.253 --> 00:14:16.188
to the caramel syrups, which
they put into their drinks.

00:14:16.355 --> 00:14:18.424
Well, in the US, you'll find caramel color

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:20.459
in the salted caramel hot chocolate

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:22.494
and the salted caramel latte.

00:14:23.062 --> 00:14:24.697
Which I drink.

00:14:24.763 --> 00:14:26.098
Caramel color is worth pointing out

00:14:26.098 --> 00:14:27.366
because it's on the state of California's

00:14:27.366 --> 00:14:29.301
Proposition 65 list of chemicals

00:14:29.301 --> 00:14:31.303
which are known to the
state to cause cancer

00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:32.504
or reproductive toxicity.

00:14:33.239 --> 00:14:35.708
Ooh, reproductive toxicity. That's fun.

00:14:35.708 --> 00:14:37.576
Um. [laughs]

00:14:37.576 --> 00:14:38.577
See, I was scared,

00:14:38.577 --> 00:14:40.746
but the good news is
there's only two types

00:14:40.746 --> 00:14:43.215
of caramel color, classes III and IV,

00:14:43.315 --> 00:14:44.350
that contain the chemical

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.318
that's to blame for this, 4-MEL.

00:14:46.752 --> 00:14:48.420
The bad news is that
class IV caramel color

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.788
does appear on the menu in the UK.

00:14:50.055 --> 00:14:51.423
While there is some evidence that suggests

00:14:51.423 --> 00:14:53.492
that the amounts currently
in our food are pretty safe,

00:14:53.492 --> 00:14:55.928
the state of California
banning it isn't a great look.

00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.730
Meanwhile, at a federal level,

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:01.634
the FDA still says that there
is "no reason to believe

00:15:01.634 --> 00:15:04.570
that there are any immediate
or short-term health risks

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:09.008
presented by 4-MEI at the
levels expected in food."

00:15:09.008 --> 00:15:11.577
So, kind of up to you.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:14.647
They're lying. We shouldn't
be putting this out there!

00:15:15.114 --> 00:15:16.215
The one other thing worth pointing out

00:15:16.215 --> 00:15:17.516
is the difference between the wraps

00:15:17.516 --> 00:15:18.651
used in the two countries.

00:15:18.651 --> 00:15:20.152
There's only one wrap used in the UK,

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:21.954
and it's this one, the kibbled rye wrap.

00:15:21.954 --> 00:15:23.122
Here's the ingredients list.

00:15:24.123 --> 00:15:26.492
We also have kibbled rye wraps in the US,

00:15:26.492 --> 00:15:29.395
and the ingredients list
is virtually identical.

00:15:29.395 --> 00:15:31.630
But we can also get a plain tortilla wrap

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.766
as part of the falafel and red peppers

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:35.801
and Pret's chicken Parm wraps.

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:37.403
The ingredients list for this wrap

00:15:37.403 --> 00:15:39.405
is a little more alarming.

00:15:39.405 --> 00:15:41.073
There's three different gums in here,

00:15:41.073 --> 00:15:42.708
but it's actually the fumaric acid

00:15:42.708 --> 00:15:44.076
you may want to watch out for.

00:15:44.076 --> 00:15:47.212
It's an acidity regulator that's
pretty common in tortillas.

00:15:47.212 --> 00:15:48.380
But the European Union says

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.916
that while it's practically nontoxic,

00:15:50.916 --> 00:15:54.386
long-term exposure is
probably toxic to your kidneys

00:15:54.386 --> 00:15:55.788
due to the results of studies

00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:58.357
carried out on calves and rats.

00:15:58.357 --> 00:15:59.858
[laughing]

00:16:00.893 --> 00:16:02.461
Yeah, I would just not eat it.

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:04.897
I wouldn't say Pret's exciting.

00:16:04.897 --> 00:16:06.665
Like, they're just a solid option.

00:16:06.665 --> 00:16:07.599
They're there for you.

00:16:07.599 --> 00:16:09.902
No, Pret's the kind of place
you eat on accident once.

00:16:09.902 --> 00:16:12.204
And I'm very glad I didn't
have to eat any of that food,

00:16:12.204 --> 00:16:15.441
'cause it all looked bland as ♪ hell! ♪

00:16:15.441 --> 00:16:16.475
I'm singing a lot today.

00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:18.177
All right. We done.

